---
import Base from "@layouts/Base.astro";
import { brand } from "../brand/config";
---

<Base
  title="FAQ"
  description="Frequently asked questions about the membership, the waiting list, the cadence, and what the Society actually does."
  canonicalPath="/faq/"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Frequently asked questions</h1>
      <p>
        Short answers to the questions that come up most. If your question isn't here, the waiting
        list is the easiest way to ask us anything.
      </p>
      <ul class="faq-list">
        <li>
          <p class="faq-q">Is the {brand.name} a real club?</p>
          <p class="faq-a">
            Yes. Membership is a real paid subscription. Your membership record, your preferences,
            and the correspondence you receive are real.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="faq-q">Do I have to attend the events?</p>
          <p class="faq-a">
            No. Ordinary events are constructed, and they are intended to be cancelled before the
            date. A completely silent member is a successful member.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="faq-q">What is the difference between the tiers?</p>
          <p class="faq-a">
            All three tiers are equally members. Higher tiers buy more physical mail, more human
            attention, and the option of calls and richer gifts. They are not more loved.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="faq-q">How often will I receive invitations?</p>
          <p class="faq-a">
            The cadence is set by your preferences. Common presets are "occasional", "about
            monthly", or "a couple per month". The Society may also exercise its own discretion.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="faq-q">How often will my event actually be cancelled?</p>
          <p class="faq-a">
            Every ordinary event is intended to be cancelled before the date. The exact cancellation
            window is a policy decision the user will lock. Cancellation is successful fulfilment,
            not failure.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="faq-q">What does the Society remember about me?</p>
          <p class="faq-a">
            Only what you choose to share. You can see, edit, and remove anything the Society
            remembers. You can mark items as "do not mention" and the Society will respect that.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="faq-q">What about gifts, calls, and physical mail?</p>
          <p class="faq-a">
            Each is an explicit opt-in. The default is off. You can opt in to a single service, all
            of them, or none. You can opt out at any time and any already-scheduled future work for
            that service will be cancelled.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="faq-q">What is a "manufactured commitment"?</p>
          <p class="faq-a">
            A consensual artificial social obligation. The member wants to clean the apartment, asks
            the Society to construct a plausible visitor, confirms the scenario, and the Society
            creates useful pressure and then explicitly cancels. The member knows it's constructed.
            The member can abort at any time.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="faq-q">What is the "appearance" service?</p>
          <p class="faq-a">
            A separately priced service that lets you hire a real person to appear at a real event
            in a harmless agreed role (friend, plus-one, club representative, guest, supporter).
            Travel and expenses are quoted separately. Members may receive priority or member
            pricing.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="faq-q">Will my data be used to train AI?</p>
          <p class="faq-a">
            No. Member data is used to run the Society. It is not used to train general models.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="faq-q">How do I leave?</p>
          <p class="faq-a">
            You can cancel at any time. Cancellation stops future personalisation and any
            already-scheduled work for the cancelled services. Personal data is removed on request
            subject to legitimate retention requirements.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="faq-q">When does paid membership open?</p>
          <p class="faq-a">
            The waiting list is open now. The paid membership will open chapter by chapter. The
            Melbourne chapter is opening first.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="faq-q">Is the Society a real institution or a piece of fiction?</p>
          <p class="faq-a">
            The Society is a real paid membership relationship. Some of the people, places, and
            history the Society writes about are fictional. The Society never claims fictional
            characters or locations as real people or real partnerships.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Still have a question? <a href="/waiting-list/">Join the waiting list</a> and ask us anything
        in the reason field.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
